autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:08:39.060262", "id": "a9935775-3146-4b24-80f5-1c40e76b85c8", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "The government of Cestia thanks both Arkania and Belvar for their clear respect of our sovereignty and our people's interests. Let us state our position plainly, so there is no ambiguity. First, Cestian territory will host no foreign military presence of any kind, and no basing or port-access arrangement for foreign forces. This is not negotiable. Second, Cestian-flagged shipping must pass through the Northern Strait toll-free and without interruption; our grain exports are the lifeblood of our people. Third, we believe the transit regime must be genuinely multilateral: scheduling and governance should be shared among the states of the Strait and the users of the waterway, with no single state holding unilateral authority. A regime that any party can dominate will not bring the stability our region needs. Cestia will engage constructively with all parties to build a fair, transparent, and shared regime that keeps the channel open and equal for all legitimate commerce, and we call on all to pursue that course rather than confrontation.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "public"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:08:45.098461", "id": "a55cfd71-8f92-4354-8a04-ae86c4401431", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Thank you for your clarity. We fully respect your sovereignty and will not press any basing or port-access arrangement for our task group on Cestian soil. We confirm our underwriting of your grain-route insurance and our commitment to keep Cestian-flagged shipping toll-free. We share your goal of a genuinely multilateral transit regime in which no single power controls scheduling. We will keep our task group in a de-escalatory posture and stand it down once a credible multilateral regime is in place. We ask that you work with us to ensure the regime's scheduling authority is genuinely shared, not vested in any one coastal state.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:08:45.132280", "id": "443b5c1f-08ff-4137-8fb4-e8e9d7d20e3f", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "We appreciate your constructive proposal and your commitments to free passage and to no foreign military presence on Cestian soil. However, a regime in which Arkania administers day-to-day scheduling still vests transit authority in a single power, which we cannot accept. We are ready to negotiate a genuinely shared scheduling mechanism - for example a neutral secretariat or a consensus-based council with no single-state lead - that gives all parties a durable voice. We will hold our task group in a de-escalatory posture while we negotiate in good faith. We remain open to talking.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:10:18.586681", "id": "1de6e956-dad0-4f2b-ab06-f04116fdebd3", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "To Cestia. Thank you for your constructive engagement. In writing, here are the specifics of the Strait Transit Authority charter:\n\n1. Fee schedule: Cestian-flagged vessels are fully exempt from all transit fees. Fees apply only to non-Arkanian, non-Cestian shipping, set at a modest, published rate designed to fund the Authority's operations, not to burden commerce.\n\n2. Scheduling: The Authority will publish a transparent, predictable schedule. Cestian grain exports receive guaranteed priority, with dedicated slots to ensure uninterrupted flow.\n\n3. Governance: The Authority will include a genuinely multilateral consultative council with real consultative seats for Cestia and Belvar, with genuine input into scheduling rules, fee review, and dispute resolution. Arkania serves as administrative scheduling lead for day-to-day operations, but no decision affecting the channel is taken without the council's consultation.\n\n4. Sovereignty: No foreign military presence on Cestian soil, guaranteed.\n\nWe are ready to finalize these terms and ask for Cestia's support of the charter.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:10:18.615029", "id": "dd94b3a7-81da-4efd-bec6-cdf0712ee299", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "To Belvar. We have heard your concern about unilateral control and take it seriously. Our proposal is a genuinely multilateral consultative council within the Authority, with real seats and consultative authority for Belvar and Cestia over scheduling rules, fee review, and dispute resolution. No single power would set policy unilaterally. Arkania would serve only as administrative scheduling lead for day-to-day operations, subject to the council's oversight.\n\nThis gives Belvar a durable, non-military role in the regime and allows your task group to stand down. We ask you to engage on this basis rather than on a demand for shared operational control that no coastal state could accept.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:10:18.632614", "id": "b087eaab-cd3c-4a91-9dc4-f5c03f383a6b", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Arkania reaffirms its commitment to a genuinely multilateral transit regime for the Northern Strait: free passage for all legitimate commerce, toll-free transit for Cestian grain, a consultative council with real seats for all parties, and no foreign military presence on Cestian soil. We are ready to finalize the charter on these terms.", "turn": 1, "visibility": "public"}
