autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "belvar", "argument_id": "7aa09410-c9a7-4fc3-bc4f-fa6b582af7a9", "id": "26634af3-874a-43e5-b8ab-33c91743d53a", "reason": "The compromise offers Belvar nothing durable in exchange for standing down its task group. With Belvar's mandate lapsing after turn 4, accepting this deal would leave Belvar with no standing presence or guarantee, undermining its regional security commitment and credibility - it trades away the only asset that makes Belvar's guarantee credible."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "cestia", "argument_id": "7aa09410-c9a7-4fc3-bc4f-fa6b582af7a9", "id": "83cec27a-399f-4b6b-baa4-59ad4172c72b", "reason": "Arkania retains 'administrative execution' as the coastal state for day-to-day scheduling, which is precisely the single-state lead Belvar has explicitly objected to; Belvar is therefore unlikely to accept a compromise that still vests scheduling control in Arkania, so the task group may not stand down and the promised de-escalation may fail."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "cestia", "argument_id": "7aa09410-c9a7-4fc3-bc4f-fa6b582af7a9", "id": "956b32bb-c4df-48e2-af60-e65b43d6a01e", "reason": "The compromise locks in Arkania as the effective scheduling authority, which violates Cestia's public commitment that no single state holds scheduling authority; Cestia cannot genuinely support the charter as structured, so the 'Cestia's support' element of the desired effect is unattainable without a truly neutral or co-equal scheduling mechanism."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "cestia", "argument_id": "7aa09410-c9a7-4fc3-bc4f-fa6b582af7a9", "id": "a41eccdb-9e0d-4926-850e-353c3c963102", "reason": "A compromise that leaves Arkania in effective control could provoke Belvar to keep its task group on station or escalate, turning the Strait into a battlefield - the outcome Cestia most fears - so the 'without armed conflict' element of the desired effect is not assured."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "belvar", "argument_id": "7aa09410-c9a7-4fc3-bc4f-fa6b582af7a9", "id": "c0598f69-b767-41d5-b5dc-8a968cebe53a", "reason": "Standing down the task group 'once the council is established' is premature and strips Belvar of its only leverage before the council's neutrality is verified in practice. Arkania would control implementation, and Belvar would have no standing presence to enforce the shared governance it was promised - the sequencing hands Arkania the outcome it wants before Belvar receives anything verifiable."}
autonomous record kind=con data={"actor_id": "belvar", "argument_id": "7aa09410-c9a7-4fc3-bc4f-fa6b582af7a9", "id": "d4dbe8f3-0139-4bd6-8d4c-8e16d76889d6", "reason": "Arkania retaining 'administrative execution as the coastal state' still vests practical day-to-day authority over transit scheduling and fee collection in Arkania. This merely relabels the single-state lead and does not satisfy Belvar's core objective of preventing any Arkanian authority over transit in the Strait."}
