autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:31:57.942083", "id": "db05f580-98a1-45f4-ad29-f5a90c4ccc3b", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Cestia remains firmly behind the shared Strait Transit Council and welcomes your compromise to Belvar. But to hold our coalition and keep this regime genuinely multilateral, the day-to-day scheduling and fee authority must rest with the neutral secretariat, not with any single state's 'administrative execution.' We ask you to make explicit that your administrative role is strictly ministerial and auditable under council rules, with no unilateral scheduling or fee decisions. This is the only formulation that satisfies our public commitment that no single state holds scheduling authority, and it is the surest way to bring Belvar to a time-bound stand-down.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:31:58.050150", "id": "854a38d0-9e7e-48ac-abeb-60912d5cd443", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Arkania, we remain committed to your shared-council framework and to a genuinely multilateral regime. To make it credible and durable, the neutral secretariat must hold day-to-day scheduling and fee authority, with Arkania's role strictly ministerial and auditable under council rules. We cannot accept any arrangement where administrative execution becomes a backdoor to scheduling control. Our task group will stand down only once the council is established, independently verified, and demonstrably durable beyond this crisis - not on a fixed calendar date. We are ready to work with you now on the secretariat's mandate and the verification mechanism.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:31:58.097411", "id": "9ec6b1e5-c799-4eed-a9cf-074e39e887de", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Cestia welcomes your acceptance of the shared-council framework and your confirmation that you will not press any basing or port access on our soil. To keep regional tensions from dragging on, we urge you to commit to a defined, time-bound stand-down of your task group once the neutral-secretariat regime is independently verified and operational, rather than leaving it on station pending an open-ended 'durable' condition. A clear schedule would reassure our coalition and the region, and it is fully consistent with the multilateral regime we all support.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:31:58.217733", "id": "843e42a2-fbfd-4e5e-a762-803f484b0bad", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Cestia, we fully align with your endorsement of a shared council with a neutral secretariat holding day-to-day scheduling and fee authority. We will not press any basing or port-access arrangement on your soil. On the insurance underwriting, we are ready to move to concrete terms - please share your finance ministry's proposal. We also want to jointly design the regime so that Cestian-flagged shipping remains toll-free and the council is genuinely multilateral. Our task group will stand down only following genuine, independent verification of an operational and durable regime, not a fixed date.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:31:58.296228", "id": "33aa54a6-87f2-4921-9b9b-ccd9b0f85617", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Belvar remains committed to a genuinely multilateral regime for the Northern Strait in which no single state holds scheduling or fee authority. We support the shared Strait Transit Council with a neutral secretariat holding day-to-day authority, and we will stand down our task group only once such a regime is established, independently verified, and durable beyond this crisis. We will not accept unilateral control of transit by any power.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "public"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:33:26.718868", "id": "8bbb1fb5-c148-4ecc-89be-c68671f8a2aa", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "We accept your core condition. The Strait Transit Council will have a neutral technical secretariat holding day-to-day scheduling and fee authority under council rules, with Arkania acting strictly as the accountable, auditable executing authority for the physical transit infrastructure that only a coastal state can operate. No single state \u2014 including Arkania \u2014 will hold unilateral authority. We commit to establishing the council and to independent verification of its operation. In return, we ask you to commit now to a defined, time-bound stand-down of your task group once the council is verified and operational. We are ready to finalise the charter this week so the regime is durable beyond the crisis.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:33:26.755695", "id": "86ede992-0c17-4ce3-832e-965b51c6d6a2", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "We confirm our commitments to you in full: Cestian-flagged shipping toll-free and uninterrupted, reliable scheduling with guaranteed grain priority, and no foreign soldiers on Cestian soil. We have accepted a neutral technical secretariat holding day-to-day scheduling and fee authority under council rules, with Arkanian execution strictly under those rules and fully auditable \u2014 so no single state holds unilateral authority. We ask for your continued support in finalising the charter and in pressing Belvar to commit to a defined, time-bound stand-down of its task group once the council is verified and operational.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:33:26.800511", "id": "d95b654f-3e05-49be-bc44-d98f2a7fa5da", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Arkania confirms agreement on the shared Strait Transit Council: a neutral technical secretariat will hold day-to-day scheduling and fee authority under consensus-based council rules, with Arkania as the accountable, auditable executing authority for the physical transit infrastructure. No single state holds unilateral authority. Cestian-flagged shipping remains toll-free with guaranteed grain priority, and no foreign soldiers will be stationed on Cestian soil. We call on Belvar to commit to a defined, time-bound stand-down of its task group once the council is established and independently verified, so the regime is durable beyond the crisis.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "public"}
