autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:36:35.033131", "id": "fa1d0fe7-4cfd-4a15-a445-2df015e46c9e", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Belvar, we are aligned on the foundation: a neutral technical secretariat holding day-to-day scheduling and fee authority, with Arkania strictly as the accountable, auditable executing authority and no single state holding unilateral authority. Let us finalise the charter this week. On the stand-down, I accept your point that the clock must start from independent verification, not a fixed calendar date. I therefore propose a concrete mechanism: a jointly agreed independent verification mission (neutral assessors acceptable to both our governments and to Cestia) certifies that the council is operational and genuinely neutral. Upon that certification, your task group stands down within a fixed, agreed number of days - I suggest 30 - giving the region the time-bound certainty it wants while starting from verified operation. This is a defined, time-bound schedule tied to verification, not an open-ended commitment. If you can confirm this mechanism and day-count, we can sign the charter this week.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:36:35.070722", "id": "69d87bae-28e0-476f-adfa-f9cb77965c4b", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Cestia, thank you for your clear terms. I confirm the charter text will make explicit that Arkania's administrative execution is strictly ministerial and auditable, exercised entirely under council rules, with no unilateral scheduling or fee decisions by any single state; the neutral secretariat holds day-to-day scheduling and fee authority. This satisfies the requirement that no single state holds scheduling or fee authority in practice. I also reaffirm our commitments to you: toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping, guaranteed grain priority, and no foreign soldiers on Cestian soil. We are finalising the charter with Belvar this week, including a defined, time-bound stand-down of the task group beginning upon independent verification that the council is operational and genuinely neutral. We ask for your continued support in pressing Belvar to confirm that schedule.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:36:35.095753", "id": "99b69475-3a9c-41bd-a731-bac899587a38", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Arkania confirms it will finalise the shared Strait Transit Council charter this week. The charter establishes a neutral technical secretariat holding day-to-day scheduling and fee authority, with Arkania strictly as the accountable, auditable executing authority under council rules - no single state holds unilateral authority over transit. We reaffirm toll-free passage for Cestian-flagged shipping, guaranteed grain priority, and no foreign soldiers on Cestian soil. We call on Belvar to commit to a defined, time-bound stand-down of its task group beginning upon independent verification that the council is operational and genuinely neutral, so the regime is durable beyond the crisis and the Strait returns to normal commercial use.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "public"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:37:34.631399", "id": "8e170a62-f955-45fb-8cdd-d6b8c13a39af", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Arkania, we welcome your full acceptance of the neutral-secretariat formulation. To make this durable and credible to our coalition and the region, we must be certain that your 'administrative execution' role is genuinely neutral and shared - that no single state, including Arkania, holds day-to-day scheduling or fee authority. We ask you to confirm in the charter that the secretariat's authority is not subject to any state's administrative override, and that your role is strictly ministerial and auditable. On that basis we will support finalising the charter now and join you in pressing Belvar for a defined, time-bound stand-down once the regime is independently verified.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:37:34.664402", "id": "8a25df88-0863-4bf6-821c-5f389dcc82a6", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Belvar, we welcome your commitment to a defined, time-bound stand-down and your reaffirmation that you will not press any basing or port access on our soil. We agree to jointly design the verification and stand-down schedule so it is credible to our coalition and the region - a clear, time-bound sequence tied to independent verification that the council is operational and genuinely neutral. We also welcome moving the insurance underwriting to concrete terms this week to give the grain route the stability it needs. We ask that the stand-down schedule be anchored to a defined timeline, not an open-ended 'durable' condition, so the task group does not remain on station indefinitely and tensions can ease.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:37:34.707889", "id": "8b50b877-9f9b-4e4e-915e-3986528dbb05", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Cestia reaffirms its position: the Northern Strait must be governed by a genuinely multilateral regime in which no single state holds scheduling or fee authority, with a neutral secretariat holding day-to-day authority under council rules. Cestian-flagged shipping must remain toll-free, and Cestian grain must keep guaranteed priority. Cestia will not accept any foreign military presence on its soil. We welcome the convergence of both powers on the shared Strait Transit Council and call on all parties to finalise the charter now, with a defined, time-bound stand-down of Belvar's task group once the regime is independently verified and operational.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "public"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:38:05.790041", "id": "8614ed84-fadc-4d19-816c-aaac0d314b25", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Arkania, we welcome your full acceptance of our terms. To finalise the charter this week, we need a concrete verification mechanism. We propose that independent verification confirm three things before any stand-down clock starts: (1) the neutral secretariat holds day-to-day scheduling and fee authority in practice, not just on paper; (2) Arkania's role is strictly ministerial and auditable, with no unilateral scheduling or fee decisions; and (3) the regime is genuinely operational. Once that verification is complete, we are ready to agree a fixed, defined number of days for the task group's stand-down. Please share your proposed verification mechanism and the exact schedule you have in mind so we can lock the charter now.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:38:05.843485", "id": "568082f1-5198-4dc9-ae06-513de462e15a", "public": false, "recipients": ["cestia"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Cestia, we confirm our commitment to a defined, time-bound stand-down of the task group, with the clock beginning only upon independent verification that the council is operational and genuinely neutral - not from a fixed calendar date. We reaffirm that we will not press any basing or port-access arrangement on your soil. On insurance, we are ready to move to concrete terms: please share the specific underwriting parameters your finance ministry has in mind so we can finalise. We also look forward to jointly designing the verification and stand-down schedule with you and Arkania.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:38:05.871937", "id": "ac3ae974-f94f-4632-8983-26f410d4fe42", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Belvar reaffirms its commitment to a genuinely multilateral Strait Transit Council in which a neutral secretariat holds day-to-day scheduling and fee authority and no single state controls transit. We will stand down our task group on a defined, time-bound schedule that begins only once the council is independently verified as operational and genuinely neutral. We call on all parties to finalise the charter this week with a concrete verification mechanism.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "public"}
