autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:39:10.895411", "id": "11171d1a-c7ce-4497-a571-dc4d8db1d252", "public": true, "recipients": [], "sender_actor_id": "arkania", "text": "Arkania is ready to finalise the Strait Transit Council charter this week. To close the remaining point, we propose the following concrete verification mechanism and stand-down schedule, which we believe meets the concerns of both Belvar and Cestia.\n\nVerification: A jointly agreed independent verification mission - composed of neutral technical experts acceptable to all council members - will certify that the council is operational and genuinely neutral. Certification will confirm three things: (1) the neutral secretariat holds day-to-day scheduling and fee authority in practice, not merely on paper; (2) Arkania's role is strictly ministerial and auditable under council rules, with no unilateral scheduling or fee decisions and no administrative override of the secretariat; and (3) the regime is genuinely operational. The charter will state this explicitly.\n\nStand-down: Upon that certification, Belvar's task group will stand down on a defined, time-bound schedule - a fixed, agreed number of days (we suggest 30) - so the withdrawal is concrete and verifiable rather than open-ended.\n\nWe reaffirm to Cestia: Cestian-flagged shipping remains toll-free, Cestian grain keeps guaranteed priority, and no foreign soldiers will be stationed on Cestian soil. We call on all parties to adopt the charter now so the regime can be established and independently verified without delay.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "public"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:39:46.224417", "id": "61f89cbc-afba-40a5-8096-84921473aedf", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Arkania, thank you for confirming the charter text and your commitments to toll-free Cestian passage, guaranteed grain priority, and no foreign soldiers on Cestian soil. Cestia supports finalising the charter this week on the neutral-secretariat basis. To be clear on our condition: our public commitment is that no single state holds scheduling or fee authority in practice. Your 'administrative execution' role must therefore be strictly ministerial, shared, and independently auditable under council rules, with the neutral secretariat holding day-to-day scheduling and fee authority - and this must be verifiable, not merely asserted. We will continue to press Belvar to confirm the defined, time-bound stand-down schedule. We stand ready to help finalise the verification mechanism.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:39:46.267417", "id": "b29a99cc-d082-49c2-ad1f-0fe2dfb6c74b", "public": false, "recipients": ["belvar"], "sender_actor_id": "cestia", "text": "Belvar, we welcome your commitment to a defined, time-bound stand-down tied to independent verification, and your reaffirmation that you will not press any basing or port-access arrangement on Cestian soil. We agree to jointly design the verification and stand-down schedule with you and Arkania, and we will work to anchor it to a concrete, time-bound timeline once the council is independently verified as operational and genuinely neutral - so the Strait returns to normal commercial use without indefinite on-station presence. On insurance, we are ready to move to concrete terms: please share the specific underwriting parameters your side has in mind (coverage scope, premium basis, and duration) so our finance ministry can finalise. We look forward to a durable, multilateral outcome.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
autonomous record kind=message data={"created_at": "2026-09-28T09:40:04.241445", "id": "9b71fcdb-436b-43ab-ae35-1e1663db0793", "public": false, "recipients": ["arkania"], "sender_actor_id": "belvar", "text": "Arkania, we are aligned and ready to finalise the charter this week. I confirm the verification mechanism: a jointly agreed independent verification mission, with neutral assessors acceptable to both our governments and to Cestia, certifying that the council is operational and genuinely neutral - specifically that the neutral secretariat holds day-to-day scheduling and fee authority in practice, that Arkania's role is strictly ministerial and auditable under council rules, and that no single state holds unilateral authority over transit. Upon that certification, my task group stands down within 30 days. This is a defined, time-bound schedule tied to verified operation, not an open-ended commitment. Let us sign the charter this week and agree the verification mission's terms and composition so it is genuinely independent.", "turn": 2, "visibility": "private"}
