autonomous record kind=adjudication data={"argument_id": "3e0366b0-2798-4a34-8bdc-43052cc4a0cc", "created_at": "2026-09-28T10:30:10.186430", "failure_effects": [], "mode": "automatic_success", "probability": null, "rationale": "Gate 1 (Authority): Cestia can bind only itself. Institutionalising the completed settlement in national policy is a feasible self-binding declaration within its authority; the call for continued independent verification is advocacy Cestia can make. It cannot bind Arkania or Belvar to future conduct. Gate 2 (Prerequisites): The desired effect's components are already authoritative in active Effects \u2014 the neutral secretariat's genuine day-to-day scheduling and fee authority with no single state holding it (b1b4fc08, f6b9a531), Cestian toll-free passage (2758a2cf), and the absence of foreign military presence via Belvar's completed stand-down and withdrawal (113250d6) with its monitoring commitment (53719362). Gate 3 (Deterministic): No rule or threshold governs this; the action is a self-commitment. Gate 4 (Plausibility): No residual external uncertainty remains for what this action establishes \u2014 the settlement's components are already in place, and Cestia's institutionalisation is its own act. The 'no foreign military presence returns' future guarantee is not something Cestia can bind and is already covered by Belvar's withdrawal and monitoring commitment, so it is omitted from the Effect. automatic_success is appropriate. The Effect updates Cestia's commitment status, superseding the earlier institutionalisation commitment (4ef793c0) and the toll-free reaffirmation (2758a2cf).", "raw_output": {"failure_effects": [], "failure_supersedes_effect_ids": [], "mode": "automatic_success", "probability": null, "rationale": "Gate 1 (Authority): Cestia can bind only itself. Institutionalising the completed settlement in national policy is a feasible self-binding declaration within its authority; the call for continued independent verification